Only the debug-profile Rust [38;5;10m.so[0m diverged: on a NULL [38;5;10msci[0m, C dies with [38;5;10mSIGSEGV[0m while Rust died with [38;5;10mSIGABRT[0m, because Rust's [38;5;10mdebug_assertions[0m-gated UB check reported a null dereference. This translation must reproduce accesses that are UB by Rust's rules — the C indexes [38;5;10msci->bitalloc[i][0m up to [38;5;10mi == 509[0m on a 64-byte array and has no null checks — so I disabled [38;5;10mdebug-assertions[0m and [38;5;10moverflow-checks[0m in both profiles. [38;5;10msrc/lib.rs[0m needed no change; it was already a faithful translation, including the unsigned wrap in [38;5;10mcode % mod - mod / 2[0m, the masked shift counts, and [38;5;10mbs->pos[0m advancing on the reject path.[0m[0m
