Two design points were load-bearing. Every call runs in a [38;5;10mfork()[0med child on shared memory, so rows that crash on purpose — the C's [38;5;10mint[0m overflow makes the guard miss and it dereferences [38;5;10mbuf + 234881024[0m — can be compared by [3mfatal signal[23m instead of taking the runner down. And the working region is bracketed by a 512 MiB [38;5;10mPROT_NONE[0m reservation, wider than the [38;5;10mbuf ± 256 MiB[0m a 32-bit [38;5;10mbs->pos[0m can reach, so that wild access faults identically for both libraries rather than randomly hitting some unrelated mapping.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
As an extra check beyond the spec, the suite also passes against a [38;5;10m-O3[0m C rebuild (made from a copy outside [38;5;10mc_src/[0m, which I did not modify), confirming the reproduction of the C's undefined shifts does not depend on the ground-truth build's optimization level.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Two caveats worth stating plainly: the masked-shift and signed-overflow behaviours are x86-64 properties that both toolchains happen to agree on, not guarantees — on a different architecture these would need re-verification. And the crash-parity rows assert that both libraries fault the same way, which is agreement on undefined behaviour rather than on defined semantics.[0m[0m
